## Dependency Notes

- The existing SQLite substrate is the required foundation; MongoDB, a server process, hosted
  authentication, and background-daemon dependencies are out of scope.
- Database authority covers Tool Shed-generated work collateral, its structured lifecycle state,
  body content, revisions, relationships, and reconciliation data. Source code, tests, canonical
  product documentation, imported owner material, selected external evidence, provider
  instructions, and portable recovery artifacts remain file-owned under an explicit contract.
- Generated lifecycle paths are presentation only. They cannot become artifact identity,
  relationship targets, or a second writable authority.
- Ordinary Codex work must not require SQL. Managed commands must provide compact bounded context
  and revision-fenced temporary Markdown editing projections with transactional apply.
- Conversion is additive and reversible until parity, backup, rollback, rebuild, upgrade, and
  client qualification gates pass. Retiring original collateral is a separate retention decision.
- The live database remains untracked. Git checkpoints must be deterministic, reviewable, and
  policy-driven rather than emitted for every read or routine write; GitHub is optional.
- Terminal child work, an empty queue, a database transaction, or a release does not by itself
  satisfy the outcome. Universal closed-loop reconciliation must propagate verified results to
  this map and the source Idea Brief.

